---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/justuno';
const title = "Justuno for Shopify: visitor capture, identity and delivery handoff";
const desc = "Evaluate popup and quiz data quality, the supported Shopify installation and the first permitted message after capture.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I install Justuno from its Shopify listing?",
    "answer": "The reviewed listing reports that it is currently unavailable. Confirm a supported installation route with Justuno; the listing status does not establish a company shutdown."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does visitor identification create SMS consent?",
    "answer": "No. Keep identified profiles separate from documented SMS subscriptions and let the destination sender check eligibility before dispatch."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a Justuno pilot prove?",
    "answer": "It should prove that useful visitor preferences reach the intended profile with permission evidence, that interrupted handoffs recover without duplicate messages, and that additional contribution justifies capture costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">App directory</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Operating review · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Confirm installation before designing acquisition</h2>
    <p>At this review, the <a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/justuno-social-email-leads">Pop-Ups &amp; Spotlight by Justuno listing</a> says it is not currently available on the Shopify App Store and directs support questions to Justuno. That is an installation constraint, not evidence that the company has shut down. Ask Justuno which supported connection applies to your store before replacing a working installation.</p>
    <h2>What Justuno adds to a sending program</h2>
    <p><a class="link" href="https://www.justuno.com/">Justuno currently promotes popups and Spotlight visitor identification</a>. Its useful role is learning who visits and what they want, then handing usable information to the appropriate destination. Treat a captured profile, an identified visitor and a subscribed SMS contact as different states. A matched email address alone does not establish permission to send marketing texts.</p>
    <h2>Design a visitor-field contract</h2>
    <p>The <a class="link" href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/487-how-to-set-up-a-shopping-preference-quiz">shopping preference quiz documentation</a> describes property elements and a Klaviyo sync workflow. A preference question can make a welcome more relevant without promising a sales lift. Before publishing, name the destination field, allowed values, blank-value behavior and owner for every answer. Keep preference, identity and channel permission in separate fields.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance case: partial and returning visitors</h2>
    <p>Use a new visitor who answers a gift-recipient question, accepts email and declines SMS. Inspect the saved answer and destination subscription states. Then return with the same email and a changed preference: the intended update should occur without another welcome or a revived SMS subscription. Repeat on mobile with an abandoned second step. A quiz completion should not be inferred from a first-step email capture.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance case: delivery retries</h2>
    <p>Trace one submission from form version and timestamp to the receiving profile and first eligible message. In a controlled test connection, interrupt delivery and restore it. Record whether the integration retries, what remains queued and how failures become visible; these are questions to verify, not claimed Justuno guarantees. A replay should preserve the original permission evidence and avoid duplicate welcomes. Assign an operator to unresolved handoffs rather than treating the popup success screen as delivery confirmation.</p>
    <h2>Respect the integration boundary</h2>
    <p>Justuno’s <a class="link" href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/491-syncing-listrak-to-justuno">Listrak instructions</a> distinguish email and SMS credentials and require an email field for phone collection in that integration. This is a concrete example of why a connector name is insufficient. Demonstrate the exact destination, required identifiers and field mapping for your chosen sender. Do not assume another connector shares those requirements or that downstream opt-outs return automatically.</p>
    <h2>Proposed experiment: relevance versus friction</h2>
    <p>Compare a short email form with a preference question against the current form, using a stable visitor assignment. Keep the incentive and traffic sources comparable. Count eligible visitors, completed captures, correctly delivered preferences and subsequent net contribution per assigned visitor. A longer quiz could improve relevance while reducing completion; inspect both effects before expanding it. These are proposed measurements, not results from a store or a test we performed.</p>
    <h2>Budget for useful profiles, not raw matches</h2>
    <p>Request current terms for traffic, capture, identity resolution, integration access and implementation work, plus the receiving sender’s charges. Model a peak acquisition month and a month with weak traffic quality. Compare incremental contribution per assigned visitor after merchandise costs, fulfillment, returns, incentives and incremental software/support costs. If discounts and refunds already reduce net sales, do not deduct them again. Divide total incremental program cost by additional usable, permitted profiles only when that denominator is positive.</p>
    <h2>Launch and rollback ownership</h2>
    <p>Before live traffic, approve a field map, a form version and a receiving flow. Exercise a purchase during the welcome delay and an opt-out before a delivery retry. The sender should recheck eligibility at dispatch. Keep a rollback that disables the new capture route without replaying stale events. If existing forms already supply sufficient data, improving their handoff may be more useful than adding another capture layer.</p>
    <h2>Next decision</h2>
    <p>Use the <a class="link" href="/guides/list-growth">list growth guide</a> for acquisition planning and <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">channel coordination</a> for dispatch ownership. Compare <a class="link" href="/apps/privy">Privy’s account-continuity review</a> when installation continuity is the main problem. Justuno’s distinct evaluation here is visitor-field quality, failed-delivery recovery and the economics of extra acquisition friction.</p>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
